(window.PF_CAT_SHARD=window.PF_CAT_SHARD||{})["76451"]={"OO0562":{"i":"OO0562","entryRequirements":"Candidates must complete the first year of the programme with at least a B average grade, to be eligible for entry into year 2.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this programme will be exposed to principles and practices of systematically developing robust and secure software. The programme will graduates with conceptual and practical skills and knowledge of software development, and will enable them to be work ready, and develop competency in pursing research in the software engineering domain.","graduateProfile":"Internal assessment, examinations","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0562"},"WI0350":{"i":"WI0350","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Engineering or Bachelor of Engineering with Honours, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have a thorough understanding of foundation engineering principles and the ability to acquire new knowledge. They will have specialist knowledge and practical engineering skills in a given engineering area,and be able to apply those skills. They will be able to communicate clearly and effectively in a professional and technical context, using appropriate media, with their colleagues and clients. They will also be able to systematically and creatively design systems that provide appropriate practical solutions to engineering problems, including being able to define needs and source appropriate data to service those needs.","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI0350"},"VI002M":{"i":"VI002M","entryRequirements":"A bachelors degree with an average grade of B or better in a discipline other than software development, computer science, or related subject, and a basic level of programming skill.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have some of the technical knowledge and skills to develop practical software systems, using a range of software technologies and tools. Graduates will be able to assist programmers/software developers. Some graduates may continue to the Postgraduate Diploma in Software Development (VI002L) or the Master of Software Development (VI002A). The PGCertSwDev also acts as an exit qualification from these.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI002M"},"VI002A":{"i":"VI002A","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree with an average grade of B or better in a discipline other than software development, computer science, or related subject, and a basic level of programming skill.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have the technical knowledge and skills to develop practical software systems, be able to independently learn and use new software technologies and tools, and have the professional and enterprise skills necessary for working effectively in ICT organisations. The MSwDev is intended to lead to working as a professional in the IT industry, but graduates seeking further qualifications could progress to a research-based master's degree. Graduates will be able to work as programmers/software developers or closely related positions in the IT industry.","graduateProfile":"Graduates will have the technical knowledge and skills to develop practical software systems, be able to independently learn and use new software technologies and tools, and have the professional and enterprise skills necessary for working effectively in ICT organisations. The MSwDev is intended to lead to working as a professional in the IT industry, but graduates seeking further qualifications could progress to a research-based master's degree. Graduates will be able to work as programmers/software developers or closely related positions in the IT industry.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI002A"},"AU5582":{"i":"AU5582","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand university entrance qualification or an approved alternative. Must meet entry requirements of each component degree. Selection criteria apply.","strategicPurposeStatement":"BE(Hons)/BSc graduates will demonstrate knowledge and understanding of the content and application of elements of both Engineering and Global Studies disciplines.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5582"},"CN0641":{"i":"CN0641","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand university entrance qualification or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be able to demonstrate and apply advanced theoretical and practical knowledge of a field of Engineering to develop practical solutions to Engineering problems to the level required for professional membership of Engineers New Zealand, employment as professional engineers and further specialised postgraduate study. They will be able to communicate clearly and effectively in a professional and technical context with their colleagues and clients. They will also be able to demonstrate introductory knowledge of and an ability to apply and communicate effectively scientific principles and concepts; in-depth knowledge and skill in a subject major; an ability to solve problems through the application of scientific knowledge and experimental skills.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0641"},"AK3751":{"i":"AK3751","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand university entrance qualification or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"BE(Hons) graduates will have an understanding of engineering fundamentals, problem solving, design, research, risk management and professional responsibility. They will develop professional capabilities in their chosen field including complex business and project management techniques. Graduates will also be prepared for postgraduate study in their chosen field.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK3751"},"CN0626":{"i":"CN0626","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Enginering with Honours or Bachelor of Engineering or other appropriate degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have an advanced knowledge of theory and research in fire engineering. They will demonstrate advanced knowledge of the fundamental principles and application of these principles to fire engineering. They will be able to communicate in a clear and concise manner and undertake independent study. They will be able to apply their knowledge to new and complex engineering problems and demonstrate an ethical approach to engineering practice.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0626"},"CN0698":{"i":"CN0698","entryRequirements":"A relevant approved bachelor's degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The MAerospaceEng programme graduates will have gained mastery of the knowledge and competencies in aerospace. In addition, they will be able to consider the wider impacts of aerospace topics from both ethical, societal, and environmental standpoints. The graduates' skills and ability to apply their knowledge will grow the capabilities of the aerospace engineering profession in New Zealand and internationally. The breadth and depth of disciplinary knowledge and practice will be solidified through the research thesis.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0698"},"AU5599":{"i":"AU5599","entryRequirements":"A BE or BE(Hons) or equivallent with a GPA  <5, or a BE or BE(Hons) or equivallent with a GPA  <3 ot its equivalent and at least  yars relevant work experience, or a relevant bachelor's degree with a GPA , 5 in 75 points above Stage II.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGCertEqEng graduates will have an improved understanding of the New Zealand geological, seismological and design context for earthquake engineering. They will have advanced knowledge and strengths in some specialist areas and be able to apply this knowledge in a sophisticated design.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5599"},"AK3732":{"i":"AK3732","entryRequirements":"A four-year bachelor's degree in engineering or equivalent","strategicPurposeStatement":"MEngSt graduates will have advanced knowledge and understanding in their chosen area of engineering. They will be able to engage analytically, critically and reflectively in their chosen field of engineering study. They may progress to further study at master's level.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK3732"},"AU5707":{"i":"AU5707","entryRequirements":"Assessment methods include exams, tests, essays, presentations, group and practical projects.","strategicPurposeStatement":"BC/BE(Hons) graduates will demonstrate knowledge and understanding of the content and application of elements of both Communication and Engineering disciplines.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5707"},"VI005J":{"i":"VI005J","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor's degree is required with an average grade of B+ or better in the relevant subjects such as environmental sciences, climate change science, chemistry, physics, electronics and computer science, architecture, building science, or design.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates with a Master of Renewable Energy degree will have a sound knowledge of the principles of a range of different energy generation, conversion, storage, transmission/distribution, and usage technologies, particularly renewable and sustainable energy technologies. Graduates will understand the environmental, economic, and societal impacts of technological decisions in energy systems. Graduates that undertake the Renewable Energy Systems Engineering major will be","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI005J"},"OO0026":{"i":"OO0026","entryRequirements":"Bachelor's degree of acceptable alternative.  Preferred qualifications are Bachelor of Surveying or postgraduate diploma in Science (Surveying)","strategicPurposeStatement":"This degree involves supervised research in a chosen surveying topic. Graduates will have advanced knowledge in the field, and the ability to study independently, and to carry out original research to internationally recognised standards.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0026"},"AU5737":{"i":"AU5737","entryRequirements":"Completed the requirements for a Bachelor of Engineering or Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) with a minimum GPA or completed the requirements for a relevant Bachelors degree with a minimum GPA.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGDipMedicalEng graduates will build on previous skills and develop an improved understanding in biomechanical engineering, medical devices, digital technology, biomaterials, and biomedical science. This will equip and enable them to apply their knowledge in settings such as the Medical, Health and Technology sectors. Graduates will acquire the skills for further postgraduate study.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5737"},"CN0676":{"i":"CN0676","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Engineering with Honours or Bachelor of Engineering, or other appropriate degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates from this degree will demonstrate advanced knowledge of the fundamental principles, and application of these principles, to transport engineering. Graduates will be able to communicate in a clear and concise manner and undertake independent study. They will be able to apply their knowledge to new and complex transport engineering problems and demonstrate an ethical approach to engineering practice.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0676"},"AU5510":{"i":"AU5510","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Engineering, Bachelor of Engineering (Honours), Bachelor of Science (Honours), Bachelor of Science, Postgraduate Diploma in Science.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the MEnergy programme will be equipped with the technical, economic, environmental, regulatory and business knowledge required for innovation in the energy field. These graduates will fill a demand for these skills and knowledge as identified by the energy industry.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5510"},"MY0350":{"i":"MY0350","entryRequirements":"Appropriate Bachelor degree or diploma or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be able to create new knowledge, critically evaluate information and communicate effectively, and be prepared for doctoral study or employment. They will have good quantitative skills, be able to solve a range of both theoretical and practical problems, have acquired the ability to work independently and with groups and, where relevant to the discipline, be able to design experiments and analyse data appropriately.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0350"},"AU5670":{"i":"AU5670","entryRequirements":"Completed either the requirements for the Degree of Bachelor of Engineering or Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) with a minimum Grade Point Average (GPA) or a relevant Bachelors degree with a minimum GPA.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGCertAerospaceEng graduates will have knowledge and competencies in sub-disciplines within aerospace engineering. Graduates will know and be able to apply several of the principles, concepts and techniques used in aerospace systems development. They will be critical and reflective, able to consider some technical and ethical aspects of aerospace engineering in New Zealand and internationally.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5670"},"AU5751":{"i":"AU5751","entryRequirements":"Completed the requirements for a Bachelor of Engineering or Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) with a minimum GPA or completed the requirements for a relevant Bachelors degree with a minumum GPA.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGCertCivilEng graduates will know, understand, and be able to apply principles, concepts and ideas into the context of civil engineering to deliver successful project outcomes. They will be able to undertake the design and construction of civil engineering infrastructure for the benefit of society.","graduateProfile":"Assessments will be a combination of coursework assignments, projects and exams.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5751"},"AU5594":{"i":"AU5594","entryRequirements":"This is an exit qualification. Students need to have been  enrolled in the MEnergy and passed at least 30 points for that degree, and been recommended for admission by the Dean or nominee","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGCertEnergy graduates will be aware of the technical, economic, environmental, regulatory and business knowledge required for innovation in the energy field. They will fill a demand for these skills and knowledge as identified by the energy industry.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5594"},"CN0636":{"i":"CN0636","entryRequirements":"A relevant Bachelor's degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will demonstrate advanced knowledge of the fundamental principles and application of these principles to fire engineering. Graduates will be able to communicate in a clear and concise manner and undertake independent study. They will be able to apply their knowledge to new and complex fire engineering problems and demonstrate an ethical approach to engineering practice.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0636"},"AU0028":{"i":"AU0028","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand university entrance qualification or an approved alternative. Must meet entry requirements of each component degree. Selection criteria apply.","strategicPurposeStatement":"BE(Hons)/BSc graduates will demonstrate knowledge and understanding of the content and application of elements of both Engineering and Science disciplines.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU0028"},"AU5757":{"i":"AU5757","entryRequirements":"\"Completed the requirements for a Bachelor of Engineering, Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) or other relevant degree with a minimum GPA, or completed the requirements for a relevant Bachelors degree and passed 60 points of relevant courses with a minimum GPA. \"","strategicPurposeStatement":"\"MProfEng graduates will know, understand, and be able to apply the principles, concepts and ideas that define their chosen engineering specialisation. They will be proven, critical, reflective practitioners able to pursue the highest personal professional goals. They will be qualified to work in the following professional roles: * Civil Engineer * Professional Engineer * Construction Engineer * Infrastructure Engineer \"","graduateProfile":"Assessments will be a combination of coursework assignments (individual and group) and exams.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5757"},"AU5672":{"i":"AU5672","entryRequirements":"Completed the requirements for either a Bachelor of Engineering or Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) with a minimum Grade Point Average (GPA) or a Bachelor of Engineering or Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) and passed 60 points in the Postgraduate Certificate in Engineering or Postgraduate Diploma in Engineering or Postgraduate Certificate in Robotics and Automation, or Postgraduate Diploma in Robotics and Automation in a relevant subject with a minimum GPA.  Or a relevant Bachelors degree and at least three years of relevant professional experience or a relevant Bachelors degree and a Postgraduate Diploma in a relevant subject with a minimum GPA.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MRobotEng graduates will know, understand and be able to apply the principles, concepts and techniques used in robotics and automation systems. They will be able to design and implement solutions at a system-level. They will be critical, reflective engineers who consider both the technical and ethical aspects of robotics and automation.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5672"},"CN0686":{"i":"CN0686","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Engineering with Honours or Bachelor of Engineering, or other appropriate degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates from this degree will demonstrate advanced knowledge of the fundamental principles, and application of these principles, to fire engineering. Graduates will be able to communicate in a clear and concise manner and undertake independent study. They will be able to apply their knowledge to new and complex fire engineering problems and demonstrate an ethical approach to engineering practice.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0686"},"MY0176":{"i":"MY0176","entryRequirements":"Master's degree in Education, Psychology, Counselling, Social Work, Speech Language Therapy, or related relevant discipline, having achieved a grade average of at least a B; 60 credits of approved undergraduate psychology; and relevant professional experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Certificate in Educational and Developmental Psychology possess essential knowledge and skills in professional practice in educational and developmental psychology. They demonstrate skills in the integration and application of educational, developmental, and psychological discipline knowledge and research. Their ability to assess, analyse, and interpret educational, developmental, and psychological knowledge ensures cultural and contextual relevance in supporting the lifelong learning of 21st century citizens. Graduates are distinguished by their development of key skills and abilities for the critical application of discipline knowledge and research.    Graduates will possess the necessary foundations to pursue further postgraduate study for professional practice in Psychology, Educational and Developmental Psychology, Education and related fields. The qualification provides a pathway to professional training in educational and developmental psychology where graduates already possess a related and relevant masters degree.  Graduates will develop skills and experience that will enhance and advance their careers in the following areas:    * Inclusive and special education (early childhood to tertiary)  * Professional development and human management within organisations   * Leadership and consultation in educational settings  * Behaviour and learning support work and specialist education support  * Community support and consultation roles","graduateProfile":"NA","educationPathway":"NA","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0176"},"MY0059":{"i":"MY0059","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand University Entrance qualification or equivalent. Must include Physics, Mathematics with Calculus and Chemistry.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Bachelor of Food Technology with Honours graduates will be competent in a range of pure and applied science, engineering, business and entrepreneurial skills. They will be innovative, and will be leading change agents in the food industry.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0059"},"AU5554":{"i":"AU5554","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand university entrance qualification or an approved alternative, and a minimum number of credits in specified subjects. Selection is based on results from prior study, and the evaluation of supplementary material related to the music major.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will demonstrate knowledge and understanding of the content and application of elements of both Engineering and Music disciplines.","graduateProfile":"NA","educationPathway":"NA","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5554"},"AU5753":{"i":"AU5753","entryRequirements":"Completed the requirements for a Bachelor of Engineering or Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) with a minimum GPA or completed the requirements for a relevant Bachelors degree with a minumum GPA.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGDipCivilEng graduates will know, understand, and be able to apply principles, concepts and ideas into the context of civil engineering to deliver successful project outcomes. They will be reflective practitioners, able to undertake the design and construction of civil engineering infrastructure for the benefit of society and exercise ethical decision-making.","graduateProfile":"Assessments will be a combination of coursework assignments, projects and exams.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5753"},"AU5532":{"i":"AU5532","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelors degree or bachelors (honours) degree in Arts, Commerce, Engineering, Health Sciences,  Law, Planning, or Science with a minimum Grade Point Average (GPA), or its equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MDisMgt graduates will have a unique blend of understanding that emphasises imaginative thinking as well as sound knowledge and technical skills.    Development across a wide variety of subject areas will ensure that they can apply the desired knowledge and skills in a range of complex disaster situations. In addition to core disaster management knowledge, a number of subject areas will extend the development of disaster management professionals with a holistic, yet balanced mix of disaster management related content.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5532"},"CN0665":{"i":"CN0665","entryRequirements":"An approved Bachelor's degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Postgraduate Certificate in Product Innovation holders will have a wide knowledge of product innovation at an advanced level and a thorough knowledge of the process of innovation. They will be able to apply research and writing skills, and their knowledge of product innovation, to working in a range of professional, commercial, consultancy, community, government, educational, or higher-education academic contexts.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0665"},"AU0393":{"i":"AU0393","entryRequirements":"A four year Bachelor of Engineering or Bachelor of Engineering (Honours); or other approved bachelors degree and three years of relevant work experience; and a minimum Grade Point Average (GPA).","strategicPurposeStatement":"ME graduates will have a specialised knowledge within a particular engineering discipline. They will have demonstrated the ability to conduct and report on a piece of research at an advanced level.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU0393"},"AU5673":{"i":"AU5673","entryRequirements":"Completed either the requirements for the Degree of Bachelor of Engineering or Bachelor of Engineering (Honours)  in a relevant subject with a minimum  Grade Point Average (GPA) or completed the requirements for a relevant Bachelors degree with a minimum GPA.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGCertRobotEng graduates will know and be able to apply many principles, concepts and techniques used in robotics and automation systems. They will be critical, reflective engineers who consider both the technical and some ethical aspects of robotics and automation.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5673"},"CN0632":{"i":"CN0632","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand university entrance qualification or equivalent","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be able to demonstrate and apply advanced theoretical and practical knowledge of a field of Engineering to develop practical solutions to Engineering problems to the level required for professional membership of Engineers New Zealand, employment as professional engineers and further specialised postgraduate study. They will be able to communicate clearly and effectively in a professional and technical context with their colleagues and clients. They will also have the conceptual and theoretical knowledge of leadership & organisation, science & performance, teaching & learning, and society and culture to develop the health and well-being for all in Aotearoa | New Zealand through sport and physical activity. In addition to specialised knowledge in a discipline, graduates will be skilled in equity, diversity and inclusion, biculturally confident and competent and experienced in diverse sporting workplaces and organisations.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0632"},"CN0696":{"i":"CN0696","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Engineering with Honours or Bachelor of Engineering, or other appropriate degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates from this degree will demonstrate advanced knowledge of the fundamental principles, and application of these principles, to engineering management. Graduates will be able to communicate in a clear and concise manner and undertake independent study. They will be able to apply their knowledge to new and complex engineering management problems and demonstrate an ethical approach to engineering practice.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0696"},"AU5139":{"i":"AU5139","entryRequirements":"Bachelors degree or overseas equivalent or a professional qualification or experience in engineering","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGCertLMRTech will have an advanced understanding of concepts in chemical and materials engineering specific to light metals reduction technology, especially aluminium.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5139"},"WI0953":{"i":"WI0953","entryRequirements":"Bachelors degree or equivalent, completed at a specified minimum level of attainment.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates from the Master of Engineering Practice will have technical expertise at an advanced level, advanced management and professional practice skills, the ability to solve complex, real-world engineering problems and the ability to design, develop and manage complex technical projects.","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI0953"},"AU5622":{"i":"AU5622","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand university entrance qualification or an approved alternative. Selection criteria apply.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be proficient in a range of contemporary design methodologies and technologies, and be able to apply design thinking and practice to create new products, services and systems on behalf of industry, society and the economy. They will be creative, entrepreneurial practitioners able to pursue personal professional goals and postgraduate study.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5622"},"AK1320":{"i":"AK1320","entryRequirements":"A relevant three-year bachelor's degree, bachelor degree with honours or a postgraduate diploma with a B grade average in papers at level 7 or above.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Analyses evolving concepts, theories, tools and practices of transmedia, understood here as the creation and circulation of narrative content across multiple media formats, networks, devices and technological platforms.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1320"},"MY0148":{"i":"MY0148","entryRequirements":"(a) meet the University admission requirements as specified, and  (b) have been awarded or qualified for a Bachelor of Aviation, Bachelor of Aviation Management or equivalent degree or qualification, having achieved a grade average of at least a B- in the highest level papers.","strategicPurposeStatement":"To introduce advanced aviation topics for students engaged in the aviation industry.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0148"},"AU5590":{"i":"AU5590","entryRequirements":"Completed the requirements for a Bachelor of Engineering or Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) or another relevant bachelors degree with a minimum Grade Point Average (GPA)","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGCertEPM graduates will know, understand, and be able to apply principles, concepts and ideas relevant to project, programme and portfolio management across a range of industries. Graduates will be eligible to seek registration with the PMI.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5590"},"AU5600":{"i":"AU5600","entryRequirements":"BSc in Earth Sciences or Geology, BAdvSci(Hons), BSc(Hons), PGDipSci in a relevant specialisation, or BE or BE(Hons) with a relevant specialisation, with a GPA of 5.0 or higher.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the MEngGeol will have received sound training in both engineering geology and related geoscience subjects and will be equipped with the knowledge and skills required to pursue a career in ground engineering. They will be able to apply their skills and knowledge in an ethical and professional manner. MEngGeol graduates will be sufficiently prepared for an accelerated pathway towards Engineering New Zealand's (formerly IPENZ) 'Chartered Member (Engineering Geologist)' qualification [CMEngNZ (PEngGeol)].","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5600"},"AU5674":{"i":"AU5674","entryRequirements":"Completed either the requirements for the Degree of Bachelor of Engineering or Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) in a relevant subject with a minimum Grade Point Average (GPA) or the completed requirements for a relevant Bachelors degree with a minimum GPA","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGDipRobotEng graduates will know and be able to apply many principles, concepts and techniques used in robotics and automation systems. They will be critical, reflective engineers who consider both the technical and some ethical aspects of robotics and automation.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5674"},"AU5579":{"i":"AU5579","entryRequirements":"Exit qualification only. Students must have previously been enrolled in the Master of Disaster Management.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGCertDisMgt graduates will have a blend of understanding that combines independent thinking as well as sound disaster management related skills. Competences developed across a wide variety of subject areas will ensure that graduates from the programme can apply knowledge in a range of complex disaster situations.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5579"},"AU0059":{"i":"AU0059","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand university entrance qualification or an approved alternative. Prior study in specific subjects is required. Selection criteria apply.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The BE(Hons) is a professionally accredited degree which not only provides graduates with technical and theoretical knowledge and analytical, problem-solving and communication skills required by the profession of engineering but also prepares them to be adaptive, independent and creative in applying the knowledge and skills in a wide range of careers.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU0059"},"AK1317":{"i":"AK1317","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelor's degree with honours or equivalent and relevant engineering or managerial work experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MEPM graduates will be engineering professionals with advanced leadership and managerial skills required to undertake complex engineering projects. They will have an advanced understanding of the full scope of project management. They may also progress to further study at master's level and beyond.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1317"},"CN0697":{"i":"CN0697","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Engineering with Honours or Bachelor of Engineering, or other appropriate four-year degree. Relevance and standard of previous study are the main criteria for approval.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates from this degree will demonstrate advanced knowledge of the fundamental principles, and application of these principles, in engineering. Graduates will be able to communicate in a clear and concise manner and undertake independent study. They will be able to apply their knowledge to new and complex engineering problems and demonstrate an ethical approach to engineering practice.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0697"},"MY0360":{"i":"MY0360","entryRequirements":"(a) meet the University admission requirements as specified; and  (b) have been awarded or qualified for a Bachelors with Honours degree in food engineering, food science or food technology, or equivalent, or   (c) have been awarded a Bachelor's degree in engineering, science, technology, or equivalent and completed at least 36 months  relevant professional experience in the food or biological products industry.","strategicPurposeStatement":"On successful completion of the Master of Food Safety and Quality graduates will be well able to manage and lead food safety and quality projects in the food industry. Graduates will be able to identify the risks to food safety and quality and describe the critical parameters in food processing that need to be controlled to ensure food safety and quality. Graduates will have extensive theoretical knowledge, practical skills and discipline specific competencies that will enable them to take up professional roles in the food industry or to continue with further postgraduate research in the area of food science and technology.  The Master of Food Safety and Quality can be a terminating qualification for industry-orientated learners who wish to lead and manage food safety and quality programmes or a successful graduate could progress to doctoral study in the area of food technology .  We expect the majority of students will be studying while employed in the food industry. However those that are not may use this degree as a way of entering the food industry at a reasonably advanced level. The degree will be applicable to all sectors of the food industry from the manufacture of different commodity and consumer products to regulatory authorities, testing facilities and other companies providing support to the food industry.","graduateProfile":"NA","educationPathway":"NA","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0360"},"CN0677":{"i":"CN0677","entryRequirements":"An approved Bachelor's degree.\tArchitectural engineering, structural engineering, building services and energy engineering, integrated building design.\t1","strategicPurposeStatement":"The MArchEng will produce graduates who: are engaged in the building industry and their profession; have the technical knowledge and skills required for professional registration at CPEng level, when endorsed with Structural Engineering or Building Services and Energy Engineering; have the technical expertise and interdisciplinary knowledge required for technical design leadership of the design of sustainable sustainability of buildings and retrofit developments;  can work effectively with other design professionals and project stakeholders to collaboratively develop integrated solutions to complex built environment design challenges; can apply independent thinking and advanced knowledge and skills of buildings to the technical design and construction of new and existing buildings.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0677"},"CN0625":{"i":"CN0625","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Engineering with Honours in an appropriate subject or Bachelor of Science with Honours in an appropriate subject","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have gained advanced theoretical and practical knowledge in preparation for higher-level employment opportunities or for entry to further postgraduate study. They can apply independent thinking and advanced knowledge and skills to the development and remediation of civil infrastructure systems.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0625"},"AU4067":{"i":"AU4067","entryRequirements":"A BE or BE(Hons) from the University of Auckland with a minimum Grade Point Average (GPA); or the equivalent; or other approved bachelors degree and three years of relevant work experience and a minimum GPA.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MEngSt graduates will demonstrate an advanced level of knowledge within a chosen engineering discipline.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU4067"},"AU5755":{"i":"AU5755","entryRequirements":"Completed the requirements for a Bachelor of Engineering, Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) or other relevant degree with a minimum GPA or completed the requirements for a relevant Bachelors degree and passed 60 points in postgraduate certificate or postgraduate diploma in a relevant subject with a minimum GPA, or completed the requirements for a relevant Bachelors degree, and a relevant Postgraduate Diploma with a minimum GPA, or completed the requirements for a relevant Bachelors degree with a minimum GPA and have at least three years of relevant professional experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the Master of Civil Engineering will have mastery of knowledge and be able to apply theories, concepts and practices into the context of civil engineering and against risk to deliver successful project outcomes. They will be critical, reflective practitioners, able to undertake the design and construction of civil engineering infrastructure for the benefit of society and exercise ethical leadership in engineering decision-making and/or pursue further advanced academic studies.","graduateProfile":"Assessments for the courses will be a combination of coursework assignments, projects and exams.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5755"},"AU0013":{"i":"AU0013","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand university entrance qualification or an approved alternative. Must meet entry requirements of each component degree. Selection criteria apply.","strategicPurposeStatement":"BA/BE(Hons) graduates will demonstrate knowledge and understanding of the content and application of elements of both Arts and Engineering disciplines.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU0013"},"MY1060":{"i":"MY1060","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Engineering degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have knowledge at a high level in an engineering discipline. They will be able to critically evaluate information and communicate effectively, and be prepared for further study or employment. They will have good quantitative skills, be able to solve a range of both theoretical and practical problems, have acquired the ability to work independently and with groups and, where relevant to the discipline, be able to design experiments and analyse data appropriately.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY1060"},"AU4066":{"i":"AU4066","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Engineering or approved equivalent qualification with a GPA of 5 in the final year or a relevant bachelors degree and 3 years work experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MEMgt graduates will have developed a high level of expertise in engineering management enabling them to combine their role as professional engineers with the demands of management.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU4066"},"CN0637":{"i":"CN0637","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Engineering with First or Second Class Honours in an appropriate subject or  Postgraduate Certificate in Civil Engineering with a GPA of at least 5.0 or  Bachelor of Science with First or Second Class Honours in an appropriate subject.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this degree will have developed advanced knowledge and skills relevant to their future careers in a research or professional environment, so that they can provide leadership in a professional context and engage effectively with future research opportunities. They will be able to apply independent thinking and advanced knowledge and skills to the development and remediation of civil infrastructure systems. Graduates can engage effectively and confidently in a variety of academic and professional settings and provide expertise to support high-level decision making processes.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0637"},"CN0661":{"i":"CN0661","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand university entrance qualification or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be able to demonstrate and apply advanced theoretical and practical knowledge of a field of engineering to develop practical solutions to engineering problems to the level required for professional membership of the Institution of Professional Engineers of New Zealand. They will be able to seek employment as professional engineers and engage confidently in an Aotearoa New Zealand/Te Tiriti context, and further specialised postgraduate study. They will be able to communicate clearly and effectively in a professional and technical context with their colleagues and clients. They will also be prepared to work in New Zealand and international companies that employ creative, business-aware graduates with the knowledge of science and engineering necessary to create, develop and market technically and commercially viable products. They will be able to clearly understand and define the important elements required to address open-ended design problem/opportunity statements as well as systematically define the functional, aesthetic and financial criteria of feasible design solutions to given problem/opportunity statements. Graduates will be capable of producing and assessing design prototypes against defined solution criteria and have the confidence and ability to propose and implement innovative ideas in a commercial setting.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0661"},"CN0675":{"i":"CN0675","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand university entrance qualification or approved equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will understand the effects of the history, values, culture, language, roles and objectives of different stakeholders on a building project. They will be able to identify and communicate project objectives, constraints, site conditions and potential design issues including community and infrastructure needs and how these may be considered in the design process. They will understand factors contributing to failure and success in building project and reasons for gaps between expected and actual building performance.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0675"},"AU5722":{"i":"AU5722","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor of Engineering, Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) or other relevant Bachelors degree, with a minimum GPA.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGDipInfraAssetMgt graduates will know, understand, and be able to apply the principles, concepts and ideas that define infrastructure asset management across a range of sectors in the context of climate change and adaptation. They will be critical, reflective practitioners.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5722"},"AK3566":{"i":"AK3566","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree in engineering technology or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Holders of the PGDipEng will have advanced knowledge and skills within a specialist field of engineering practice and advanced analytical, planning and critial thinking skills. They will be prepared for further study at master's level.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK3566"},"VI002B":{"i":"VI002B","entryRequirements":"A bachelors degree with an average grade of B+ or better in an appropriate engineering discipline or in computer science, or similar subject.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have the technical knowledge and skills to solve real-world engineering problems, and have the professional, and enterprise skills necessary for working effectively as engineers in New Zealand organisations. The MEP is intended to lead to working as a professional in industry, but graduates could progress to a research based masters degree or a PhD.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI002B"},"MY0429":{"i":"MY0429","entryRequirements":"(a) meet the University admission requirements as specified; and have:  (b) been awarded or qualified with the Bachelor of Engineering with Honours or equivalent with a minimum B grade average over the highest level majoring papers; or  (c) been awarded or qualified for the Postgraduate Diploma in Engineering or equivalent with a minimum B grade average; or  (d) been awarded or qualified with the Bachelor of Engineering with Honours or equivalent and have significant professional experience; or  (e) been awarded or qualified for the Postgraduate Diploma in Engineering or equivalent and have significant professional experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"ME graduates will have knowledge at a higher level than a BE graduate in an engineering discipline. They will be able to create new knowledge, critically evaluate information and communicate effectively, and be prepared for doctoral study or employment. They will have good quantitative skills, be able to solve a range of both theoretical and practical problems, have acquired the ability to work independently and with groups and, where relevant to the discipline, be able to design experiments and analyse data appropriately.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0429"},"CN0602":{"i":"CN0602","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand university entrance qualification, or equivalent with selection to second year based on academic performance.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have a theoretical and practical knowledge of a field of engineering to the academic level required for professional membership of the Institution of Professional Engineers of New Zealand and will be ready for employment as professional engineers or for further specialised study and research in their field.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0602"},"OO0290":{"i":"OO0290","entryRequirements":"Acceptable performance in years 1 and 2 of the Bachelor of Surveying degree programme.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this degree programme will have the knowledge and research skills needed for an advanced professional or academic career in surveying.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0290"},"VI00Z9":{"i":"VI00Z9","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand university entrance qualification, or equivalent, with physics and mathematics (calculus and statistics) to NCEA level three strongly recommended.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be able to apply a sound knowledge of engineering principles and relevant science to information and communications technology. They will be able to use appropriate tools and techniques to design, construct, measure and analyse engineering solutions. They will be able to apply project management skills to the achievement of engineering and business objectives, and will be able to function at various levels within an organisation. The BE(Hons) is an accredited degree providing a pathway to professional certification. Graduates will find employment in a range of industries developing or making use of information and communication technologies. Completion of the BE(Hons) may lead to further study for a Masters or PhD degree.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00Z9"},"AU0022":{"i":"AU0022","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand university entrance qualification or an approved alternative. Must meet entry requirements of each component degree. Selection criteria apply.","strategicPurposeStatement":"BCom/BE(Hons) graduates will demonstrate knowledge and understanding of the content and application of elements of both Commerce and Engineering disciplines.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU0022"},"AU5738":{"i":"AU5738","entryRequirements":"Completed the requirements for a Bachelor of Engineering or Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) with a minimum GPA or completed the requirements for a relevant Bachelors degree with a minimum GPA.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGCertMedicalEng graduates will develop a focused set of skills chosen from health related engineering fields including biomechanical engineering, medical devices, digital technology, biomaterials, and biomedical science. This will expand their skills in the Medical, Health and Technology sectors. Graduates will acquire the skills for further postgraduate study.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5738"},"MY0060":{"i":"MY0060","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand University Entrance qualification or equivalent. Must include Physics and Mathematics with Calculus.","strategicPurposeStatement":"BE(Hons) graduates will be competent in an engineering discipline and will have skills and attitudes to comprehend and evaluate new information and concepts. They will be able to manage resources optimally through analysis, interpretation and decision making.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0060"},"WI1005":{"i":"WI1005","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand University Entrance qualification or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"This conjoint degree gives students the opportunity to complete the requirements of two component degrees over a reduced period of time. Graduates will have knowledge and skills from both Business and Engineering disciplines which will give them a firm grounding for careers in many different areas.","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI1005"},"AU5593":{"i":"AU5593","entryRequirements":"This is an exit qualification. Students need to have been  enrolled in the MEnergy and passed at least 30 points for that degree, and been recommended for admission by the Dean or nominee","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGDipEnergy graduates will have an understanding of the technical, economic, environmental, regulatory and business knowledge required for innovation in the energy field. They will fill a demand for these skills and knowledge as identified by the energy industry.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5593"},"AU5721":{"i":"AU5721","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) or equivalent with a minimum GPA, or a Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) or equivalent and passed 60 points in a specific Postgraduate Diploma or Postgraduate Certificate with a minimum GPA, or a relevant Bachelors degree with a minmum GPA and three years relevant professional experience, or a relevant Bachelors degree and a relevant Postgraduate Diploma with a minimum GPA (120-point pathway); or a relevant Bachelors degree with a minimum GPA or a relevant Bachelors degree and passed 60 points in a specific Postgraduate Diploma or Postgraduate Certificate with a minimum GPA (180-point pathway).","strategicPurposeStatement":"MInfraAssetMgt graduates will know, understand, and be able to apply the principles, concepts and ideas that define infrastructure asset management across a range of sectors in the context of climate change and adaptation. They will be proven, critical, reflective practitioners able to pursue the highest personal, professional goals and/or research studies.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5721"},"CN0667":{"i":"CN0667","entryRequirements":"An approved Bachelor's degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have a wide general knowledge of theory and practice across the field of Product Innovation. They will have a deep, thorough, and expert knowledge of the process of innovation and will have produced an extended and thorough project in product innovation practice. They will be able to apply research and writing skills, and their knowledge of product innovation, to working in a range of professional, commercial, consultancy, community, government, educational, or higher-education academic contexts.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0667"},"VI002K":{"i":"VI002K","entryRequirements":"A bachelors degree with an average grade of B+ or better in an appropriate engineering discipline or in computer science, or similar subject.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have some of the technical knowledge and skills needed to solve real-world engineering problems and will have improved their career prospects in engineering. Some graduates will continue to the Postgraduate Diploma in Engineering Practice (VI002J) or Master of Engineering Practice (VI002B); the PGCertEP also acts as a step-off qualification from the PGDipEP and MEP.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI002K"},"WI0144":{"i":"WI0144","entryRequirements":"Entry by invitation based on results of years one to three of the BE.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have appropriate practical engineering skills for their specialisation and be able to apply those skills. They will possess knowledge of science, mathematics and engineering appropriate to a professional engineer, and be able to communicate clearly and effectively in a professional and technical context, using appropriate media, with their colleagues and clients. They will also be able to systematically and creatively design systems that provide appropriate practical solutions to engineering problems, as well as able to define needs and source appropriate data to service those needs.","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI0144"},"AU5778":{"i":"AU5778","entryRequirements":"A relevant qualification and offer of PhD conditional on completion of this PGCert.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGCertBioEng graduates will know and understand bioengineering principles and approaches relevant to medical technology research, as well as their application in and translation to a clinical setting. They will be critical, reflective individuals able to pursue doctoral study in bioengineering and professional careers in the field of medical technologies.?","graduateProfile":"Assessment modes include projects, presentations, reports and assignments.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5778"},"AU5671":{"i":"AU5671","entryRequirements":"Completed either the requirements for the Degree of Bachelor of Engineering or Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) with a minimum Grade Point Average (GPA) or a  relevant Bachelors degree with a minimum GPA.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGDipAerospaceEng graduates will know and be able to apply many of the principles, concepts and techniques used in aerospace systems development. Graduates will be able to implement solutions at a component level. They will be critical and reflective, able to consider most technical and some ethical aspects of aerospace engineering in New Zealand and internationally.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5671"},"AU5723":{"i":"AU5723","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor of Engineering, Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) or other relevant Bachelors degree, with a minimum GPA.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MPGCertInfraAssetMgt graduates will know, understand, and be able to apply the principles, concepts and ideas that define infrastructure asset management across a range of sectors in the context of climate change and adaptation.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5723"},"AK1306":{"i":"AK1306","entryRequirements":"Undergraduate degree with a B average.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have undertaken a research project or sponsored industry project in the creative technologies field.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1306"},"CN0685":{"i":"CN0685","entryRequirements":"A relevant Bachelor's degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Holders of the Postgraduate Certificate will have a wide knowledge of product design at an advanced level and a thorough knowledge of the product design process. They will be able to apply research and writing skills, and their knowledge of product design, to working in a range of professional, commercial, consultancy, community, government, educational, or higher-education academic contexts.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0685"},"AU5501":{"i":"AU5501","entryRequirements":"Bachelors degree, Bachelor of Engineering or Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) at a level deemed satisfactory by the Dean of Faculty of Engineering, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGCertEng graduates will have acquired an advanced level of understanding of the theory and practice informing their engineering specialisation. The plastics specialisation provides advanced knowledge of plastics materials and processing primarily to science and engineering graduates employed by the plastics industry","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5501"},"AU5777":{"i":"AU5777","entryRequirements":"BE, BE(hons), or a relevant Bachelor's degree with appropriate GPA, or a relevant Bachelor's degree and a GradDip in Engineering Project Management, provided the qualification has not been awarded.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Postgraduate Diploma in Engineering Project Management graduates will know, understand, and be able to apply the principles, concepts and ideas that define project, programme, and portfolio management across a range of industries. They will demonstrate proficiency in applying these principles to real-world scenarios with a critical and reflective approach. Graduates will be eligible to seek registration with the Project Management Institute (PMI).","graduateProfile":"Assignments, presentations, group assignments, discussion papers, seminar papers, case studies, research project.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5777"},"CN0255":{"i":"CN0255","entryRequirements":"An approved Bachelor's degree of recognised professional discipline-specific experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have a foundational knowledge of geospatial science and technology at a postgraduate level. They will be prepared for an entry level geospatial role and also for further postgraduate study.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0255"},"VI002L":{"i":"VI002L","entryRequirements":"A bachelors degree with an average grade of B+ or better in an appropriate engineering discipline or in computer science, or similar subject.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have technical knowledge and skills in developing software systems, be able to learn and use new software technologies and tools, and be aware of issues and responsibilities when working as professionals in ICT organisations. Graduates will be able to work as programmers/software developers or closely related positions in the IT industry. Some graduates may continue to the Master of Software Development (VI002A). The PGDipSwDev also acts as an exit qualification from the MSwDev.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI002L"},"VI002J":{"i":"VI002J","entryRequirements":"A bachelors degree in any subject (except information systems or business analysis) to at least a B- average standard, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have the technical knowledge and skills to solve real-world engineering problems and have the problem-solving, team-work and communications skills for working effectively as engineers. They will have enhanced their career prospects in software engineering, network engineering, or electronic and computer system engineering. Some graduates will be able to continue to the Master of Engineering Practice (VI002B); the PGDipEP also acts as a step-off qualification from the MEP.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI002J"},"AU5669":{"i":"AU5669","entryRequirements":"Completed a BE or BE(Hons) from the University of Auckland with a minimum Grade Point Average (GPA); or the equivalent; or other approved Bachelors degree and three years of relevant work experience and a minimum GPA; or an approved pathway through a PGCert or PGDipEng or PGCert or PGDipAerospaceEng.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MAerospaceEng graduates will know, understand and be able to apply the principles, concepts and techniques used in aerospace systems development. Graduates will be able to design and implement solutions at a system level. They will be critical and reflective, able to consider both the technical and ethical aspects of aerospace engineering in New Zealand and internationally.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5669"},"AU5735":{"i":"AU5735","entryRequirements":"Completed the requirements for a Bachelor of Engineering or Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) with a minimum GPA or completed the requirements for a relevant Bachelors degree with a minumum GPA.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the PGCertMaterialsEng programme will have knowledge and competencies in sub-disciplines within materials engineering of specific value to their engineering practice. The PGCertMaterialsEng will introduce graduates to the core concepts of materials science and engineering, and will help them decide whether they want to continue study in this field. Potentially these students may also transition to either the MMaterialsEng or PGDipMaterialsEng instead of being awarded the PGCertMaterialsEng qualification.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5735"},"AU5589":{"i":"AU5589","entryRequirements":"Completed the requirements for a Bachelor of Engineering, Bachelor of Engineering (Honours), relevant postgraduate diploma, or relevant bachelors degree with a minimum Grade Point Average (GPA) or a relevant Bachelors degree or Bachelors Honours degree and the Postgraduate Certificate in Engineering Project Management with a minimum GPA. All applicants must have at least two years of relevant professional experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MEPM graduates will know, understand, and be able to apply the principles, concepts and ideas that define project, programme and portfolio management across a range of industries. They will be proven, critical, reflective practitioners able to pursue the highest personal professional goals or research studies. Graduates will be eligible to seek registration with the PMI. They will be able to apply for admission to the PhD.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5589"},"AK1325":{"i":"AK1325","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelors degree completed to a merit standard","strategicPurposeStatement":"ME graduates will have specialised knowledge and advanced practical engineering skills within a particular engineering discipline. They will be able to engage analytically, critically and reflectively in their chosen field of engineering study.They will have demonstrated the ability to conduct research and report the outcomes of their research clearly and effectively. They will be prepared for study at doctoral level.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1325"},"CN0656":{"i":"CN0656","entryRequirements":"An approved Bachelor's degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this programme will possess the knowledge and skills to select and apply relevant renewable energy engineering concepts, frameworks, and technologies, critically evaluate technical and policy outcomes, and effectively communicate findings through written reports, presentations, and technical documentation.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0656"},"CN0606":{"i":"CN0606","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Engineering with first- or second-class honours or Bachelor of Science with first- or second-class honours or, exceptionally, another appropriate degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates can demonstrate advanced knowledge of a field of Engineering; apply and communicate effectively engineering principles and concepts; understand, evaluate, access and review, critically, new information (including findings and discussions in the literature); engage in rigorous intellectual analysis, criticism and problem solving; work independently; carry out research, write a composite report and communicate effectively concepts, results, and conclusions.  \n\n\n\r\nCompletion of this degree can lead to professional employment or the possibility of doctoral study. The degree may be endorsed in bioengineering, chemical and process engineering, civil engineering, electrical and electronic engineering, mechanical engineering, or software engineering.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0606"},"AU5598":{"i":"AU5598","entryRequirements":"BE(Hons) or equivalent with a GPA  <5 in 120 points above Stage III, or, BE(Hons) or equivalent and 60 points in the PGCertEqEng, or PGCertEng with a GPA of  <5, or a relevant bachelors degree with a GPA  <4 in 120 points of the most advanced courses and 3 years of relevant professional experience, or a relevant Bachelors degree as approved by Senate and 60 points in the PGCertEqEng, or PGCertEng with a GPA of  <5.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MEqEng graduates will have a deep understanding of the New Zealand geological, seismological and design context for buildings and infrastructure subjected to strong earthquake ground shaking. They will have the capability to access the latest research and to apply the fundamentals and to undertake earthquake engineering research or complex open ended design.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5598"},"AK1296":{"i":"AK1296","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree in engineering or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGCertE graduates will have advanced knowledge and skills within a specialist field of engineering practice. They may progress to further study at postgraduate level.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1296"},"AU5577":{"i":"AU5577","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor of Engineering or Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) degree, or an equivalent degree with a minimum Grade Point Average (GPA), or another relevant degree with a minimum Grade Point Average (GPA).","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGDipEng graduates will know and understand the principles, concepts and ideas that underpin engineering. They will be critical, reflective practitioners able to pursue personal professional goals and postgraduate study. Completion with a sufficiently high GPA will also allow entry to Masters study.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5577"},"AK1440":{"i":"AK1440","entryRequirements":"In order to be admitted to the Postgraduate Certificate in Creative Technologies an applicant must have completed a relevant bachelor's degree or a relevant graduate diploma or a relevant professional qualification and professional experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"A graduate of the Postgraduate Certificate in Creative Technologies will be able to: demonstrate knowledge about the theoretical bases of creative technologies; recognise, evaluate, and respond to ethical and contextual issues in the relation between technology and society;contribute to creative technology teams, by virtue of effective collaboration and communication skills","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1440"},"CN0616":{"i":"CN0616","entryRequirements":"An approved Bachelor's degree","strategicPurposeStatement":"Master of Engineering Management graduates will be able to:  * Apply specialised knowledge in engineering management, with critical awareness of current and emerging issues relating to engineering management in New Zealand and globally;  * Utilise communication, planning, interpersonal, management and leadership skills to collaborate with people across multiple contexts;  * Independently critique, synthesise, create, integrate and use engineering and business knowledge to create value in different technological contexts.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0616"},"CN0634":{"i":"CN0634","entryRequirements":"An approved Bachelor's degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Postgraduate Diploma in Engineering Management graduates will be able to:  * Demonstrate a working knowledge of advanced topics in engineering management, with awareness of issues relating to engineering management in New Zealand and globally;  * Utilise communication, planning, interpersonal, management and leadership skills to collaborate with people across multiple contexts;  * Independently analyse, synthesise and use engineering and business knowledge to contribute to value creation in different technological contexts.  Some graduates of the PGDipEM will be able to continue to the Master of Engineering Management (MEM). The PGDipEM also acts as an exit qualification from the MEM. \n\r\nPostgraduate Diploma in Engineering Management graduates will be able to:  * Demonstrate a working knowledge of advanced topics in engineering management, with awareness of issues relating to engineering management in New Zealand and globally;  * Utilise communication, planning, interpersonal, management and leadership skills to collaborate with people across multiple contexts;  * Independently analyse, synthesise and use engineering and business knowledge to contribute to value creation in different technological contexts.  Some graduates of the PGDipEM will be able to continue to the Master of Engineering Management (MEM). The PGDipEM also acts as an exit qualification from the MEM.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0634"},"CN0621":{"i":"CN0621","entryRequirements":"Engineering, Arts","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be able to demonstrate and apply advanced theoretical and practical knowledge of a field of engineering and develop practical solutions to engineering problems to the level required for professional membership of the Institution of Professional Engineers of New Zealand. and find employment as professional engineers able to engage confidently in an Aotearoa New Zealand/Te Tiriti context, or further specialised postgraduate study. They will be able to communicate clearly and effectively in a professional and technical context with their colleagues and clients. * Be able to question and challenge, communicate, analyse, research and intelligently understand society. The breadth of the degree provides an ideal skills and knowledge base for a wide range of employment and career options or for a range of specialised postgraduate options.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0621"},"AU5733":{"i":"AU5733","entryRequirements":"Completed a Bachelor of Engineering or Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) with a minimum GPA, or completed a Bachelor of Engineering or Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) and passed 60 points, with a minimum GPA, in a Postgraduate Certificate in Engineering in a relevant subject or in a Postgraduate Certificate or Postgraduate Diploma in Materials Engineering, or completed a relevant Bachelors degree with a minimum GPA and has at least three years of relevant professional experience, or completed a relevant Bachelors degree, and a relevant Postgraduate Diploma with a minimum GPA (120-point pathway); or completed a relevant Bachelors degree with a minimum GPA, or  completed a relevant Bachelors degree and passed 60 points, with a minimum GPA, in a Postgraduate Certificate in Engineering in a relevant subject or in a Postgraduate Certificate or Postgraduate Diploma in Materials Engineering (180-point pathway).","strategicPurposeStatement":"MMaterialsEng graduates will have mastery of the knowledge and competencies in materials engineering.?In addition, they will be able to consider the wider impacts of materials science and engineering topics from both ethical and societal viewpoints. The graduates' skills and ability to apply their knowledge will improve the capabilities of the materials engineering and other relevant engineering professions in New Zealand and internationally. The expected breadth of disciplinary knowledge and practice will be less for students with the more focused research masters. Following the award of their MMaterialsEng degree, graduates may elect to pursue an academic or research career and apply to study a PhD in the area of materials science and engineering.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5733"},"AU5734":{"i":"AU5734","entryRequirements":"Completed the requirements for a Bachelor of Engineering or Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) with a minimum GPA or completed the requirements for a relevant Bachelors degree with a minumum GPA.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGDipMaterialsEng graduates?will have a subset of the skills and knowledge to make decisions on materials selection and undertake materials failure analysis, depending on which courses they have taken. Again, students in these programmes will be sought after due to their theoretical knowledge but they will have less experience in the application of the knowledge. Students may transition to the MMaterialsEng programme if desired instead of being awarded a PGDipMaterialsEng qualification, which provides an alternative entry to the Masters programme.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5734"},"MY0433":{"i":"MY0433","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) degree or suitable equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the Master of Engineering Studies will be qualified engineering professionals with the ability to apply their knowledge to real-world industrial problems. They will have high level of knowledge and understanding of an area of engineering.","graduateProfile":"Not provided","educationPathway":"Not provided","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0433"},"AU0027":{"i":"AU0027","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand university entrance qualification or an approved alternative. Must meet entry requirements of each component degree. Selection criteria apply.","strategicPurposeStatement":"BE(Hons)/BProp graduates will demonstrate knowledge and understanding of the content and application of elements of both Engineering and Property disciplines.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU0027"},"WI0855":{"i":"WI0855","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand University Entrance qualification or equivalent Note:Entry to BE(Hons) is by invitation based on results of second and third years of Bachelor of Engineering","strategicPurposeStatement":"This conjoint degree gives students the opportunity to complete the requirements of two Bachelors degrees over a reduced period of time. Graduates will have knowledge and skills from both science and engineering disciplines providing a good grounding for careers in many areas. Graduates will have appropriate practical engineering skills for their specialisation and be able to apply those skills. They will possess a knowledge of science and mathematics appropriate to a professional engineer, and be able to communicate clearly and effectively in a professional and technical context, using appropriate media, with their colleagues and clients. They will also be able to systematically and creatively design systems that provide appropriate practical solutions to engineering problems, as well as able to define needs and source appropriate data to service those needs.","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI0855"},"AU5736":{"i":"AU5736","entryRequirements":"Completed a Bachelor of Engineering or Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) with a minimum GPA, or completed a Bachelor of Engineering or Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) and passed 60 points, with a minimum GPA, in a Postgraduate Certificate in Engineering in a relevant subject or in a Postgraduate Certificate or Postgraduate Diploma in Medical Engineering, or completed a relevant Bachelors degree with a minimum GPA and has at least three years of relevant professional experience, or completed the requirements for a relevant Bachelors degree, and a relevant Postgraduate Diploma with a minimum GPA (120-point pathway); or completed a relevant Bachelors degree with a minimum GPA, or completed a relevant Bachelors degree and passed 60 points, with a minimum GPA, in a Postgraduate Certificate in Engineering in a relevant subject or in a Postgraduate Certificate or Postgraduate Diploma in Medical Engineering (180-point pathway).","strategicPurposeStatement":"MMedicalEng graduates will develop skills and expertise in biomechanical engineering, medical devices, digital technology, biomaterials, and biomedical science. They will develop research skills through an industry focused project. This will equip and enable them to apply their knowledge in settings such as the Medical, Health and Technology sectors.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5736"},"CN0687":{"i":"CN0687","entryRequirements":"An approved Bachelor's degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have a wide geneal knowledge of theory and practice across the field of Product Design. They will have a deep, thorough, and expert knowledge of their own sub-field within Product Design. They will have produced an extended and thorough piece of original research into some aspect of Product Design and be able to apply their advanced research and writing skills, and their knowledge of product design, to working in a range of professional, commercial, consultancy, community, government, educational, or higher-education academic contexts.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0687"},"AU5607":{"i":"AU5607","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand university entrance qualification or an approved alternative. Must meet entry requirements of each component degree. Selection criteria apply.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will demonstrate an advanced knowledge and comprehension of theory, applications and techniques in their chosen fields. They will demonstrate a capacity for independent research and application of knowledge and be able to analyse, synthesize, evaluate and report in a timely and professional manner.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5607"},"CN0287":{"i":"CN0287","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand University entrance qualification or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Successful completion of this programme will make graduates employment ready as effective human resource or employees with organisational psychology expertise.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0287"},"MY0377":{"i":"MY0377","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelor's degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates can apply contemporary knowledge of critical areas of aviation business mastered at the advanced level in the successful management of commercial aviation business such as airlines, airports, air navigation service providers, maintenance and other support service organizations. Graduates can critically evaluate fundamental and applied research literature in aviation management and use it to develop practical application in solving aviation organization problems. Graduates can apply advanced knowledge and skills in judgement, analytical decision making and evaluation to develop solutions to complex and dynamic problems in aviation organizations.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0377"},"CN0614":{"i":"CN0614","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Engineering or equivalent qualification or experience","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have gained advanced theoretical and practical knowledge in preparation for higher-level employment opportunities or for entry to advanced research degrees.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0614"},"VI00U9":{"i":"VI00U9","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor of Engineering with honours from Victoria University of Wellington, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have advanced-level skills in electronic and computer systems engineering, software engineering or network engineering. They will be able to plan and undertake advanced engineering projects and will be able to conduct independent research in their area of expertise. They will communicate their designs, analysis and results clearly. Graduates will be able to work in a wide variety of engineering-related industries and organisations and will have the research training to continue to a PhD in engineering.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00U9"},"CN0651":{"i":"CN0651","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand university entrance qualification or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be able to demonstrate and apply advanced theoretical and practical knowledge of a field of engineering and be able to develop practical solutions to engineering problems to the level required for professional membership of the Institution of Professional Engineers of New Zealand. Graduates will be able to seek employment as professional engineers able and engage confidently in an Aotearoa New Zealand/Te Tiriti context, and further specialised postgraduate study. They will be able to communicate clearly and effectively in a professional and technical context with their colleagues and clients. They will also be able to apply their knowledge and skills, including Indigenous knowledge/matauranga Maori, to understand how complex socio-ecological systems and processes drive (un)sustainability. They will be able to critically engage in transdisciplinary, collaborative problem solving for sustainable change. They will understand ethical, social and environmental justice issues that impact sustainability decision making, alongside gaining skills for collaboration and community engagement in a Treaty framework. Graduates will have developed written, oral and numeracy skills and competencies to research, analyse, critique and present arguments for a range of audiences.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0651"}};
